WEBVTT

00:49.841 --> 00:52.510
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS,
ORGANIZATIONS, RELIGIONS,

00:52.594 --> 00:55.388
EVENTS, AND OCCUPATIONS
IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

01:02.854 --> 01:05.565
- Are you sure it's going to rain?
- Of course.

01:05.648 --> 01:07.776
Trust me when it comes to weather.

01:07.859 --> 01:10.236
My friend works
at the Meteorological Administration,

01:10.320 --> 01:12.030
and even he asks me about the weather.

01:15.742 --> 01:17.452
I'm more accurate than them.

01:25.502 --> 01:26.795
I hope it rains a lot.

01:29.422 --> 01:32.342
It'd be awesome if I can guess
the amount of rainfall too.

01:33.968 --> 01:38.556
But if the infected break in,
we'd be attacked first, right?

01:39.349 --> 01:43.353
That still doesn't mean
you can go into someone else's house.

01:45.396 --> 01:49.651
Excuse me, you two. Please hear us out.

01:55.031 --> 01:56.574
The second floor is dangerous.

01:56.658 --> 01:58.993
Once the lobby is breached,
it'll be our house next.

01:59.077 --> 02:01.621
So we want to move to that house.

02:01.704 --> 02:04.124
Please tell her it's okay.

02:04.207 --> 02:08.253
Some jerk dumped food waste
on the first floor, so it reeks.

02:08.336 --> 02:12.090
You just needed to talk to me,
the building representative.

02:12.173 --> 02:14.759
You're saying you want to move
to the 11th floor.

02:14.843 --> 02:16.636
But isn't it locked?

02:16.719 --> 02:19.639
We cleaned Unit 1102, not long ago.

02:19.722 --> 02:21.808
The passcode is 8888. It hasn't changed.

02:21.891 --> 02:25.019
We will clean the place
when we get out in three days.

02:25.603 --> 02:28.189
So, are you against this,
building representative?

02:28.273 --> 02:31.568
There can be legal problems later on…

02:31.651 --> 02:33.611
And the 11th floor is a royal floor,

02:34.195 --> 02:36.865
so it doesn't look good
to let the cleaners live there.

02:36.948 --> 02:38.950
The residents won't like it.

02:39.033 --> 02:41.244
Then let's hear their opinions.

02:41.327 --> 02:43.872
We have a lawyer in the building too.

02:44.455 --> 02:48.167
I'd like to say it's not possible,
from a lawyer's point of view.

02:48.251 --> 02:51.838
If you go into someone else's house
without permission, it's trespassing.

02:51.921 --> 02:54.132
If two people go in,
it's special trespassing.

02:54.215 --> 02:56.384
It's not an offense unpunishable
over objection,

02:56.467 --> 02:58.970
so anyone can report it,
even if they're not the owners.

02:59.053 --> 03:01.222
You know…

03:02.098 --> 03:05.476
I'm really sorry to say this, but…

03:05.560 --> 03:09.689
If you two go up,

03:09.772 --> 03:12.692
then our house will be at the lowest.

03:12.775 --> 03:14.986
Why should we guard your house, sir?

03:15.486 --> 03:18.072
Hey, don't look at me like that!

03:18.948 --> 03:21.826
My house has two old people.

03:21.910 --> 03:27.832
Can't you young people stay at the bottom
and help us feel safe?

03:27.916 --> 03:29.042
Hey!

03:32.128 --> 03:36.507
Mr. Oh, since you came all the way here,
tell us if you have any opinions.

03:37.217 --> 03:40.720
I think you should just stay here.

03:40.803 --> 03:45.350
If you can stay here like a guard dog,

03:45.433 --> 03:48.603
the residents would feel safe,
and it'll be good.

03:48.686 --> 03:49.896
What are you saying?

03:49.979 --> 03:51.564
- What did you say?
- Calm down.

03:51.648 --> 03:52.899
Don't.

03:52.982 --> 03:55.526
Just calm down, and do the cleaning.

04:00.156 --> 04:02.575
Now, it won't be longer than three days.

04:03.243 --> 04:04.786
Let's endure it a bit longer.

04:05.954 --> 04:10.208
Everyone's already having a hard time,
so we can't give privileges only to you.

04:10.291 --> 04:12.877
More than that,
where should we throw out the trash?

04:12.961 --> 04:15.880
We left it at the emergency stairs,
but it still stinks a bit.

04:20.051 --> 04:21.261
Don't tell me

04:22.178 --> 04:24.097
you threw it out the window.

04:26.182 --> 04:27.475
Did someone really do that?

04:27.558 --> 04:28.810
I hope not.

04:31.646 --> 04:35.024
If you need more water,
put water containers on the rooftop.

04:35.108 --> 04:37.902
I already told Unit 401,
but it'll rain tonight.

04:37.986 --> 04:41.072
How do you know that?
Is the Internet working?

04:42.824 --> 04:45.910
He's the human weather center.

04:45.994 --> 04:48.830
He could've gone to the Major League,
but he had a knee injury…

04:48.913 --> 04:51.332
- That's an exaggeration…
- Oh, dear.

04:51.416 --> 04:54.210
That's too bad for a young man like you.

04:54.711 --> 04:59.007
Do some thigh workouts regularly!

04:59.090 --> 04:59.966
Yes.

05:01.134 --> 05:02.010
I should.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.470
Work out, okay?

05:07.265 --> 05:08.099
Excuse me.

05:08.850 --> 05:10.685
I have something to tell you.

05:12.687 --> 05:14.814
It's my brother.

05:29.329 --> 05:30.621
My brother isn't here.

05:32.248 --> 05:34.792
Right? He's not here.

05:37.170 --> 05:39.213
I was just worried.

05:49.515 --> 05:52.143
My brother called me.

05:53.061 --> 05:56.064
Through that yesterday,
before the electricity was cut off.

05:58.316 --> 05:59.817
He looked fine, but…

06:00.818 --> 06:02.987
He had a strong immune system
when he was a kid,

06:03.071 --> 06:05.073
and he doesn't catch colds that easily.

06:06.074 --> 06:10.203
Maybe… he's not infected.

06:16.667 --> 06:17.919
I hope he isn't.

06:43.486 --> 06:46.239
You really are the human weather center.

06:47.365 --> 06:49.700
See? I told you it'll rain.

06:50.451 --> 06:52.245
Get some more sleep. I'll go.

06:52.328 --> 06:53.663
No, I'm awake.

06:54.247 --> 06:57.291
I should go get water to flush the toilet.
It's been bothering me.

06:57.375 --> 06:59.293
And I should put the container back out.

06:59.377 --> 07:01.337
We never know when it might rain again.

07:03.214 --> 07:04.257
When will it rain?

07:06.050 --> 07:07.301
It's raining now.

07:07.385 --> 07:09.428
Evil, begone!

07:12.140 --> 07:13.766
He's driving me crazy, seriously…

07:21.691 --> 07:22.942
What is this?

07:23.025 --> 07:24.694
He's suddenly religious now.

07:24.777 --> 07:27.071
He even prays before he sleeps.

07:29.240 --> 07:30.783
Does he even know how to pray?

07:32.702 --> 07:34.120
Let's just go to the rooftop.

07:41.043 --> 07:42.336
Evil, begone!

07:54.182 --> 07:55.558
It's raining.

07:56.934 --> 07:58.895
Shall I go outside and get some water?

08:02.482 --> 08:04.692
Heavy metals, fine dust, and pollutants…

08:04.775 --> 08:06.777
I will never drink rainwater.

08:06.861 --> 08:08.946
And I will never drink
the bathtub water, either.

08:09.447 --> 08:12.783
We'll be able to go out in three days.
What's with you?

08:14.785 --> 08:16.287
We never know.

08:58.496 --> 09:00.289
Soo-min!

09:00.873 --> 09:02.458
- Oh, gosh.
- Soo-min!

09:04.252 --> 09:05.211
Soo-min!

09:07.088 --> 09:09.131
- Is that you, Soo-min?
- Hyun-kyung…

09:09.215 --> 09:11.300
What are you doing here?

09:12.301 --> 09:14.303
Wait, no. Go away!

09:14.387 --> 09:16.847
Wait, don't go! Let's talk.

09:30.820 --> 09:32.029
Are you hurt badly?

09:34.865 --> 09:36.617
Are you sure that you got the disease?

09:37.201 --> 09:38.494
I'm not sure.

09:41.414 --> 09:46.377
I just… feel weird.

09:46.460 --> 09:49.088
What about food? Did you eat anything?

10:04.562 --> 10:05.563
Excuse me.

10:06.355 --> 10:07.607
Isn't that ours?

10:08.149 --> 10:09.609
Don't you have water at home?

10:13.529 --> 10:15.364
Drinking our water without asking…

10:15.448 --> 10:17.908
Come on. Rainwater is free.

10:17.992 --> 10:19.785
You can drink more if you want to.

10:26.208 --> 10:28.919
Hey, you shouldn't just drink that.

10:30.880 --> 10:31.797
It's okay.

10:31.881 --> 10:35.051
I always drank muddy water
during tactical training, you know.

10:45.269 --> 10:46.312
UNIT 1501 KIM SE-HOON

10:47.938 --> 10:50.316
I'm sure no one will steal your water.

10:51.025 --> 10:53.527
Do you drink rainwater too?

10:53.611 --> 10:54.695
By purifying it.

10:56.238 --> 10:59.158
I have purifying tablets,
so come over if you need any.

11:01.035 --> 11:03.120
And tell your husband before you do.

11:09.627 --> 11:11.462
I'll be the one going to his house.

11:11.545 --> 11:13.172
Never go there on your own.

11:13.756 --> 11:14.965
Don't worry.

11:15.049 --> 11:18.135
He even drinks rainwater by purifying it,

11:18.219 --> 11:20.596
so I'm sure he didn't take drugs
from the gym.

11:23.182 --> 11:24.642
What do you want for dinner?

11:25.434 --> 11:26.894
But we just ate.

11:26.977 --> 11:29.897
I think of tomorrow's breakfast menu
while I eat today's lunch.

11:29.980 --> 11:32.608
Then it's more delicious
due to my expectations.

11:34.402 --> 11:36.570
- Hi.
- Hi.

11:36.654 --> 11:38.364
Are you cleaning these days too?

11:38.447 --> 11:41.534
It felt stifling just to stay at home.

11:41.617 --> 11:44.870
The building representative
also told me to work

11:44.954 --> 11:46.539
if I want to get paid.

11:47.790 --> 11:50.167
She really is mean.

11:50.251 --> 11:53.045
But I saw something weird.

11:53.671 --> 11:54.672
Like what?

12:05.975 --> 12:07.268
Where did you find this?

12:08.102 --> 12:09.728
In a trash bag.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.985
They didn't even fill up
half the trash bag.

12:16.819 --> 12:19.780
It must be someone
with lots of trash bags.

12:21.240 --> 12:22.700
What is this?

12:22.783 --> 12:24.910
Where was that trash bag?

12:24.994 --> 12:27.288
Between the third and fourth floor.

12:31.041 --> 12:32.918
But it was fine until yesterday.

12:33.586 --> 12:34.962
Don't show it.

12:35.045 --> 12:37.548
Since I'm a detective,
I'll use an advanced technique

12:37.631 --> 12:39.258
to interrogate her.

12:39.341 --> 12:43.053
Speak nicely.
I'm sure she's still shocked.

12:43.637 --> 12:44.805
Don't worry.

12:50.019 --> 12:51.437
Hi.

12:54.440 --> 12:57.485
Are you short on anything
or having other issues?

12:57.985 --> 12:59.236
Not yet.

12:59.737 --> 13:01.405
What brings you here?

13:03.449 --> 13:05.451
We're here about the trash.

13:15.044 --> 13:16.670
You threw this away, didn't you?

13:16.754 --> 13:18.088
No.

13:18.756 --> 13:20.841
I'm not injured. I mean it.

13:20.925 --> 13:24.428
- See? I'm fine, aren't I?
- It's okay.

13:24.512 --> 13:27.640
I didn't get bitten. I really am fine.

13:33.020 --> 13:34.939
An advanced investigation technique?

13:35.481 --> 13:37.566
Seriously…

13:37.650 --> 13:39.902
Hey, it's better to ask directly first.

13:43.280 --> 13:45.366
I don't think it was Ms. Na.

13:52.081 --> 13:53.332
Her brother…

13:56.418 --> 13:58.045
Where could he be now?

14:06.971 --> 14:11.016
But why did you bring me
instead of Sae-bom?

14:11.100 --> 14:13.394
You said you can't lend me your gun.

14:13.894 --> 14:18.482
Sorry, I feel anxious without my gun.

14:19.108 --> 14:20.317
That's why you're here.

14:43.215 --> 14:44.592
EMERGENCY RELIEF GOODS

14:44.675 --> 14:46.677
That's one of the boxed lunches
we gave out.

14:47.636 --> 14:48.846
Why is that here?

14:49.555 --> 14:51.265
Martial Law has been declared.

14:51.348 --> 14:53.267
It's filled with the infected outside.

14:54.518 --> 14:55.394
So?

14:55.477 --> 14:58.147
Do we have to know everything
that's happening inside?

14:58.230 --> 15:01.442
- There may be more infected people inside.
- And if we find them?

15:01.525 --> 15:03.611
What will we do then?

15:03.694 --> 15:06.322
Where would we lock them up?
We're locked in here too.

15:07.823 --> 15:10.868
Yi-hyun, we can get out in two days.

15:11.619 --> 15:14.580
Let's not stir up things
by investigating stuff, okay?

15:14.663 --> 15:18.000
We never know. What if more people
get bitten one by one and get infected?

15:18.667 --> 15:19.877
My wife…

15:20.961 --> 15:22.504
is badly ill right now.

15:23.756 --> 15:25.507
She got tested for breast cancer,

15:26.216 --> 15:27.843
and it seems like it recurred.

15:28.886 --> 15:30.554
We got a call from the hospital.

15:33.015 --> 15:36.477
We started our shop
because we thought she was cured.

15:37.895 --> 15:38.854
Yi-hyun.

15:39.897 --> 15:42.066
I need to go to my wife.

15:42.149 --> 15:47.404
You know how much my wife suffered, right?

15:53.827 --> 15:55.204
Jung-kook is right.

15:57.039 --> 16:00.250
There isn't much we can do.

16:12.680 --> 16:13.806
Give me the whole thing.

16:20.854 --> 16:24.233
Okay. Let's wait until
the disease control team comes.

16:26.944 --> 16:27.778
Okay.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.544
I don't think I can wait.

16:46.380 --> 16:48.132
Among the candidate materials
for the cure,

16:48.215 --> 16:50.426
Material 13 proved effective
in the clinical test.

16:51.218 --> 16:52.177
How effective is it?

16:52.261 --> 16:55.681
The period and frequency
of disease occurrence

16:55.764 --> 16:58.308
improved for 72% of
the infected in serious conditions.

17:14.908 --> 17:16.285
How's your thirst?

17:16.994 --> 17:18.495
I don't feel it that much.

17:18.579 --> 17:21.040
- What about my family?
- They're outside, nice and safe.

17:22.207 --> 17:23.584
Lieutenant Colonel, not yet…

17:31.091 --> 17:32.259
By the way…

17:33.218 --> 17:34.845
did you always like meat?

17:35.429 --> 17:36.513
No.

17:38.390 --> 17:40.059
I was a vegetarian, but…

17:42.186 --> 17:44.146
It looks like you've gotten a lot better.

17:51.695 --> 17:55.032
Don't worry about your family
and just focus on recovering.

18:07.044 --> 18:09.671
Yoon Sae-bom's blood analysis
isn't complete yet, is it?

18:09.755 --> 18:10.714
No, it isn't.

18:11.882 --> 18:13.467
Do the analysis in secret,

18:13.550 --> 18:16.220
and leak the info
on Material 13 to the higher-ups.

18:16.303 --> 18:19.932
But it's still at an early clinical stage.
We need more data.

18:20.015 --> 18:21.600
That's why we're doing this.

18:21.683 --> 18:25.104
Say that the clinical tests are over
and that only the final stage remains.

19:25.539 --> 19:27.166
What did you do in there?

19:27.833 --> 19:28.667
What?

19:33.046 --> 19:37.050
It was nothing.
I was just feeling a bit stuffy,

19:37.134 --> 19:39.428
and I heard this place was empty,

19:39.511 --> 19:42.014
- I should try going in there too--
- Wait.

19:50.647 --> 19:51.899
I'm sorry.

19:51.982 --> 19:53.483
My brother is in there.

20:06.997 --> 20:08.624
Mr. Na, are you in there?

20:09.249 --> 20:10.292
Are you okay?

20:13.712 --> 20:15.797
It's okay, Soo-min. You can talk to them.

20:16.423 --> 20:18.008
They're my upstairs neighbors.

20:19.468 --> 20:21.970
Yes, for now.

20:22.054 --> 20:25.015
You ate a boxed lunch
at the basement entrance, right?

20:25.098 --> 20:27.142
Did your sister give that to you?

20:27.226 --> 20:31.647
No. The doctor from the sixth floor did.

20:32.397 --> 20:34.733
He knew…

20:36.652 --> 20:37.861
that I got infected.

20:47.454 --> 20:48.705
Aren't you hungry?

21:10.852 --> 21:12.646
What did Mr. Oh say?

21:13.230 --> 21:16.358
He asked me to come inside with him,

21:16.984 --> 21:18.694
but I refused.

21:20.821 --> 21:24.741
Then he told me to think about it,
gave me a boxed lunch, and left.

21:25.409 --> 21:28.662
Why did you refuse?
I'm sure you wanted to come inside.

21:29.329 --> 21:30.455
I was scared…

21:32.416 --> 21:34.501
that I might bite people.

21:44.094 --> 21:46.972
Please stay home even
after the lockdown is over tomorrow.

21:47.764 --> 21:51.101
- Okay.
- Both you and your brother.

21:51.685 --> 21:55.439
We'll go out, explain the situation,
and bring the medical staff.

21:57.357 --> 21:59.443
Thank you for understanding.

21:59.526 --> 22:02.738
It's not because we understand.
We just have no choice.

22:02.821 --> 22:04.948
We can't kick you out anywhere.

22:06.950 --> 22:08.577
Still, we appreciate it.

22:08.660 --> 22:10.203
Thank you so much.

22:31.349 --> 22:32.559
Bo-ram.

22:33.518 --> 22:34.686
Come here for a second.

22:35.353 --> 22:36.438
Just one second.

22:49.618 --> 22:51.828
- Bo-ram.
- I'm telling you,

22:51.912 --> 22:54.623
I won't take your money, so don't worry.

22:55.123 --> 22:58.585
- I don't want to get involved anyway.
- No, that's not why…

22:59.461 --> 23:01.546
You heard the thumping last night, right?

23:04.007 --> 23:05.967
That's the sound made by the infected.

23:08.929 --> 23:11.640
I think it was my mom.
I saw a selfie she took.

23:11.723 --> 23:13.141
She had a wound on her back.

23:13.225 --> 23:17.270
She said she bumped into
some infected woman on the sixth floor.

23:17.354 --> 23:18.355
So?

23:18.438 --> 23:19.940
What do you mean, "so"?

23:20.023 --> 23:22.984
If my mom is infected,
then we can get infected too.

23:24.778 --> 23:26.530
Wait, are you scared of that?

23:26.613 --> 23:27.906
Not worried about her?

23:29.324 --> 23:32.077
If you're that scared,
lock the door and don't come out.

23:32.661 --> 23:36.373
That's not why. I'm worried about you.

23:36.456 --> 23:37.916
Worry about me? Come on.

23:37.999 --> 23:39.876
Just be nice to your parents.

23:40.585 --> 23:42.879
I would give anything
to have parents like them.

23:54.182 --> 23:56.393
When the lockdown is over tomorrow,

23:56.476 --> 23:58.311
I should go see my mom first.

23:59.896 --> 24:03.358
First Lieutenant Lee
said she's being protected, but…

24:03.942 --> 24:05.360
She'll be fine.

24:05.443 --> 24:07.946
I didn't expect to meet my mom like this.

24:12.409 --> 24:14.953
Would the US be okay?

24:15.036 --> 24:17.455
Hey, we're lucky
that we didn't schedule a wedding.

24:17.539 --> 24:20.167
Right? If this broke out
while she was on her way here…

24:20.250 --> 24:21.960
I would've been a bad son.

24:28.842 --> 24:30.427
Do you think we did a good thing?

24:31.720 --> 24:34.014
You mean the marriage?
Of course, it's a good thing.

24:34.097 --> 24:35.891
No, I mean the fourth floor.

24:35.974 --> 24:37.350
Oh, Mr. Na?

24:38.476 --> 24:40.687
Well, his condition didn't look that bad.

24:41.188 --> 24:44.107
- Maybe since he's at an early stage?
- Lieutenant Colonel Han said

24:44.191 --> 24:46.693
the thirst can be controlled
if the person has the will.

24:46.776 --> 24:50.822
Then I'll never get infected.
I'm a very determined man.

24:52.782 --> 24:54.242
I'm looking forward to it.

24:58.496 --> 24:59.539
What is this?

25:00.248 --> 25:01.458
Is this food?

25:01.541 --> 25:02.792
Indigestion meds.

25:02.876 --> 25:05.462
I had a stomachache
whenever I was nervous about my game.

25:05.545 --> 25:07.797
So I bought that
during the Italian Championships,

25:07.881 --> 25:09.633
but it's disgusting, so don't take it.

25:10.967 --> 25:14.304
I've never taken
any indigestion relievers in my life.

25:15.388 --> 25:16.723
I envy you.

25:21.228 --> 25:24.981
I can eat all the food here, you know.

25:27.567 --> 25:29.527
- It's a lot.
- It is.

25:30.111 --> 25:32.322
It includes portions for Seo-yoon too.

25:32.405 --> 25:34.991
This is what we have
even after we gave food to everyone.

25:35.784 --> 25:38.995
Let's put them back
when the lockdown is over tomorrow.

25:41.081 --> 25:43.124
What if the lockdown
isn't lifted tomorrow?

25:44.459 --> 25:46.586
We can eat those and wait.

25:48.046 --> 25:49.506
You said you're very determined.

25:56.513 --> 25:57.931
Thank you so much.

26:31.006 --> 26:32.841
OUT OF CALL RANGE
NOT A SERVICE AREA

26:52.068 --> 26:53.069
Mr. Kim.

26:53.737 --> 26:56.281
Do you want to go outside,
or stay here with Seo-yoon?

26:57.866 --> 26:58.950
Well…

27:00.493 --> 27:03.621
Someone should stay with Seo-yoon, right?

27:04.539 --> 27:06.041
Then let me borrow your gun.

27:09.961 --> 27:11.671
Sae-bom.

27:13.006 --> 27:15.175
I'm having a hard time these days.

27:18.178 --> 27:19.929
Okay, you can keep it with you.

27:20.513 --> 27:22.849
I asked you just in case.

27:24.017 --> 27:28.605
Sae-bom, the phone's still not working.
Is it going to be okay?

27:28.688 --> 27:30.106
Of course.

27:30.190 --> 27:31.858
Stay home with Mr. Kim.

27:31.941 --> 27:33.902
I'll go out and check the situation.

27:35.236 --> 27:37.781
If you think you'll get hurt,
you have to run.

27:37.864 --> 27:40.658
Don't worry. I have a good hunch
about things like that.

27:48.875 --> 27:50.335
Hi.

27:53.171 --> 27:54.339
What is this?

27:54.422 --> 27:55.757
It was here when I got here.

27:55.840 --> 27:58.385
YOU'VE GONE THROUGH SO MUCH
UNTIL THE END

28:02.472 --> 28:04.766
I didn't know
there was someone so nice here.

28:04.849 --> 28:06.559
This person must have a lot of water.

28:06.643 --> 28:09.062
It must be the young lady
on the fourth floor.

28:09.145 --> 28:11.272
She is kind and generous.

28:14.192 --> 28:17.821
Did you live well on the third floor?
After you almost got us all killed?

28:18.488 --> 28:19.656
I'm sorry.

28:27.414 --> 28:28.832
What is this?

28:28.915 --> 28:31.334
This is like an oasis in a desert. Nice.

28:31.418 --> 28:34.003
Did you prepare this,
building representative?

28:37.757 --> 28:39.884
You all went through a lot.

28:44.305 --> 28:45.598
Can I drink more than one?

28:46.182 --> 28:48.852
Yes, go ahead.

28:57.777 --> 28:58.820
Here.

29:01.030 --> 29:03.700
Take it. We're neighbors, after all.

29:07.036 --> 29:09.372
But when will the doors be opened?

29:11.291 --> 29:14.461
Let's go outside and check.
Who wants to go outside with me?

29:24.387 --> 29:25.346
Let's go.

29:35.815 --> 29:37.942
We'll have to go outside to find out.

29:39.277 --> 29:40.278
Hey, don't drink it.

29:41.488 --> 29:43.531
We never know
if someone put something in it.

29:44.115 --> 29:45.033
No way.

29:46.618 --> 29:47.452
Hey!

29:54.918 --> 29:56.044
Seriously…

30:05.470 --> 30:06.846
Are we out too early?

31:38.229 --> 31:39.814
This is not a drill.

31:40.648 --> 31:43.318
Citizens, this is not a drill.

31:44.777 --> 31:47.280
Martial Law, originally scheduled
to be lifted today,

31:47.363 --> 31:49.824
has been extended indefinitely as of now.

31:50.533 --> 31:52.118
I repeat.

31:53.077 --> 31:55.580
Martial Law, originally scheduled
to be lifted today,

31:55.663 --> 31:57.999
- has been extended indefinitely…
- Oh, Lord.

31:58.082 --> 31:59.959
- Why?
- Lord!

32:00.043 --> 32:01.753
This is not a drill.

32:01.836 --> 32:02.795
No!

32:02.879 --> 32:04.339
I repeat.

32:05.548 --> 32:08.217
Citizens, this is not a drill.

32:09.093 --> 32:11.846
Martial Law, originally scheduled
to be lifted today,

32:11.930 --> 32:14.766
has been extended indefinitely as of now.

32:16.267 --> 32:17.852
I repeat.

32:22.815 --> 32:24.400
This is not a drill.

32:25.318 --> 32:28.321
Citizens, this is not a drill.

32:37.914 --> 32:41.334
Ms. Woo said she needed
legal consulting, so came…

32:42.710 --> 32:43.795
Where's Sang-hee?

32:44.545 --> 32:46.881
She was here. Where did she go?

32:47.966 --> 32:48.800
She's there.

32:50.593 --> 32:51.761
You're here.

32:53.846 --> 32:55.598
I suffered a lot from the lockdown.

32:55.682 --> 32:57.392
I wanted to calculate the amount, so…

32:59.894 --> 33:00.895
Okay.

33:01.938 --> 33:03.356
Did you hear the announcement?

33:03.439 --> 33:05.400
Yes, we were totally shocked.

33:05.483 --> 33:06.567
Right?

33:06.651 --> 33:07.902
Right.

33:11.781 --> 33:12.991
Is the consultation over?

33:13.074 --> 33:14.492
Yes, it is.

33:15.326 --> 33:16.452
Okay, then…

33:16.953 --> 33:18.037
All right.

33:20.540 --> 33:23.209
If you need anything else,
contact me at any time.

33:23.292 --> 33:24.794
Okay, goodbye.

33:24.877 --> 33:25.878
Goodbye.

33:29.716 --> 33:31.300
Hey, don't drink that.

33:32.844 --> 33:35.388
But you put it out
so you can get along with everyone.

33:37.348 --> 33:39.559
But we can't go out now.

33:47.734 --> 33:49.152
Was he good?

33:50.903 --> 33:51.738
What?

33:51.821 --> 33:53.156
The lawyer.

33:54.741 --> 33:56.159
His legal consultation.

33:57.910 --> 33:58.828
It was so-so.

34:17.847 --> 34:19.974
Where were you? You said you'll stay home.

34:20.058 --> 34:22.018
I went to our neighbor's.

34:22.101 --> 34:25.938
I provided consultation for Sang-hee
since the Martial Law would be lifted.

34:26.022 --> 34:28.733
But then they said it won't be lifted.

34:28.816 --> 34:32.320
I did it for nothing
when I can't even get paid for it.

34:39.535 --> 34:41.037
What should we do now?

34:42.163 --> 34:43.956
Look here…

34:44.040 --> 34:45.833
Let's just go outside, okay?

34:45.917 --> 34:48.044
We can't stay like this forever.

34:48.628 --> 34:51.297
They extended the Martial Law,
so if we go outside,

34:51.380 --> 34:53.591
we could get shot immediately.

34:53.674 --> 34:56.886
By the way, about the thumping sound
in the building…

34:58.054 --> 35:00.598
It may be from outside, or the basement.

35:00.681 --> 35:01.682
My mom.

35:03.810 --> 35:05.019
I think it's my mom.

35:06.562 --> 35:08.147
My mom has a wound on her back.

35:08.898 --> 35:12.068
I saw a picture of her back that she took.

35:12.151 --> 35:14.403
You mean it?

35:14.487 --> 35:15.530
Dad,

35:16.405 --> 35:18.491
you know something's wrong
with Mom, don't you?

35:21.577 --> 35:23.246
That's psoriasis.

35:23.329 --> 35:25.331
When you get old, your skin gets dry.

35:25.414 --> 35:28.292
It's from her scratching herself.

35:29.418 --> 35:33.714
I put that on her back.
What is it called again?

35:33.798 --> 35:36.676
You know, that thing. That…

35:36.759 --> 35:37.969
Moisturizer?

35:38.052 --> 35:40.138
Yes, that. Moisturizer.

35:40.221 --> 35:43.099
I put moisturizer on her.

35:43.182 --> 35:44.100
I saw it too.

35:44.183 --> 35:45.977
She just has dry skin, that's all.

35:47.061 --> 35:48.521
We should go check.

35:48.604 --> 35:50.314
Let's hear them out first.

35:50.898 --> 35:53.317
Don't you come into my house
without permission!

35:54.193 --> 35:56.612
You do what you want to do outside!

35:56.696 --> 36:00.366
My wife and I won't come outside anymore!

36:00.449 --> 36:02.034
Damn you…

36:10.668 --> 36:12.628
We should discuss issues
about necessities.

36:12.712 --> 36:14.922
We have to give out food and necessities

36:15.006 --> 36:16.883
from the second floor to every house.

36:16.966 --> 36:18.467
What are you saying?

36:18.551 --> 36:21.304
What can we eat, then?
Are you telling us to starve to death?

36:22.221 --> 36:25.892
To be honest,
they don't even belong to you.

36:25.975 --> 36:28.311
You just took them temporarily.

36:28.394 --> 36:30.813
Hey! How can you say that?

36:30.897 --> 36:32.231
Look here.

36:32.315 --> 36:34.066
We risked our lives to bring those!

36:34.150 --> 36:36.402
Who do you think you are
to just give them out?

36:36.485 --> 36:38.237
You live here for free.

36:38.321 --> 36:40.448
- Why are you shouting?
- What?

36:40.531 --> 36:43.868
You flipped out last time,
going on about the "royal floor."

36:43.951 --> 36:46.996
Will you charge us for breathing here too?
Should we pay for air?

36:47.079 --> 36:50.416
I can't believe my generosity
gets repaid like this.

36:50.499 --> 36:54.587
- Generosity?
- Calm down, everyone.

36:54.670 --> 36:56.672
You should've gone outside that day, then.

36:56.756 --> 36:59.175
- Calm down.
- We risked our lives to bring that!

36:59.258 --> 37:00.509
We can't let her…

37:01.969 --> 37:03.012
continue like this.

37:03.596 --> 37:05.223
She'll keep causing fights.

37:05.306 --> 37:07.850
- How can you say that?
- Please calm down.

37:16.776 --> 37:17.693
Young lady.

37:19.779 --> 37:24.533
You can't stay here any longer,
so go somewhere else.

37:25.868 --> 37:29.288
- But I have nowhere to go.
- Go to the couple at Unit 501.

37:29.372 --> 37:34.460
They're nice, so they'll find you
a place to sleep.

37:35.294 --> 37:36.462
Goodbye.

37:44.637 --> 37:45.471
Honey.

37:46.514 --> 37:51.310
- Why did they summon people again?
- It's the same thing again.

37:51.394 --> 37:52.228
You…

37:56.941 --> 37:58.818
Just make some food. I'm hungry.

37:59.402 --> 38:01.153
- Where's Dong-hyun?
- That brat…

38:02.989 --> 38:05.074
I'm sure he's somewhere in the building.

38:05.157 --> 38:06.284
Right…

38:07.743 --> 38:11.789
There's a vacant unit,
so the supermarket lady will sleep there.

38:13.332 --> 38:14.500
That's good.

38:25.344 --> 38:28.597
I thought we'd be able
to take the elevator now.

38:31.183 --> 38:33.728
I must do something about those cleaners.

38:33.811 --> 38:35.313
They have no manners.

38:35.396 --> 38:37.356
But we can't kick them out.

38:44.613 --> 38:45.448
Wait!

38:47.199 --> 38:50.453
My arm!

38:52.413 --> 38:53.622
What is it?

38:55.583 --> 38:56.917
We have something to discuss.

38:59.503 --> 39:02.089
- Let's talk outside.
- Okay, thank you.

39:04.050 --> 39:04.884
Look here!

39:05.760 --> 39:06.802
What?

39:08.220 --> 39:12.058
We're already inside, so let's talk here,
where it's comfortable.

39:18.773 --> 39:20.733
We're not done cleaning yet.

39:21.734 --> 39:24.153
Are you sure you moved in to live here?

39:26.572 --> 39:29.408
We ordered furniture
and appliances in collections,

39:29.492 --> 39:30.659
but they're not here yet.

39:30.743 --> 39:33.746
Your refrigerator and microwave
are very simple.

39:34.622 --> 39:36.791
We have to live for now, at least.

39:36.874 --> 39:40.336
Maybe that's because
you weren't thinking of living here.

39:41.712 --> 39:42.963
This is yours, right?

39:45.341 --> 39:48.010
- No.
- Right here.

39:48.094 --> 39:52.264
It says "Muil Group Construction
in Commemoration of Selection," right?

39:52.348 --> 39:56.102
They gave them out when it was chosen
to construct this apartment complex.

39:56.185 --> 40:00.648
Everyone who bought
an apartment here has it.

40:02.358 --> 40:04.443
The regular apartments, I mean.

40:04.527 --> 40:06.529
Not those who got it for free.

40:06.612 --> 40:08.656
We know you gave water to Kim Seung-beom.

40:11.617 --> 40:12.701
Who said that?

40:12.785 --> 40:13.744
Your job is to become

40:13.828 --> 40:16.997
the resident representative
and embezzle apartment funds, right?

40:17.498 --> 40:19.792
And Mr. Kim came in here
to help you with that.

40:23.629 --> 40:25.256
Do you have evidence?

40:29.510 --> 40:30.845
Let's go.

40:31.345 --> 40:32.596
Ma'am.

40:33.472 --> 40:34.807
I'll promise you one thing.

40:35.558 --> 40:37.143
You will never become

40:38.352 --> 40:40.020
the resident representative.

40:47.111 --> 40:48.821
The advanced investigation technique!

40:48.904 --> 40:49.989
It was pretty good.

40:50.573 --> 40:52.741
See? You should ask directly.

40:52.825 --> 40:54.368
If you don't, they play dumb.

40:54.452 --> 40:55.369
Right.

40:56.704 --> 40:57.788
Mr. Kim.

40:57.872 --> 40:59.457
Are you guys here to pray too?

40:59.540 --> 41:00.833
I don't have a religion.

41:00.916 --> 41:01.750
I see.

41:03.878 --> 41:04.795
What about Seo-yoon?

41:04.879 --> 41:08.549
Bo-ram from the supermarket came up,
so I asked her to stay with her.

41:09.133 --> 41:12.136
She said she left the third floor
and had no place to sleep.

41:12.219 --> 41:13.637
- Then Seo-yoon--
- Make it quick.

41:13.721 --> 41:15.931
- Okay, I'll be back soon.
- Okay.

41:16.891 --> 41:18.309
We'll head home first.

41:21.020 --> 41:24.440
What about Bo-ram? Should we tell her
to stay at Unit 502 for a while?

41:24.523 --> 41:25.900
After we ask Seo-yoon first.

41:27.067 --> 41:29.361
That's obviously a cult. I'm worried.

41:29.445 --> 41:31.489
He needs something to depend on, at least.

41:31.572 --> 41:33.574
I did that too
when I couldn't play baseball.

41:33.657 --> 41:34.867
Did you pray too?

41:34.950 --> 41:36.535
No, I did something else.

41:40.289 --> 41:42.958
Do you have drinks?
The ones in plastic bottles.

41:43.042 --> 41:44.835
Not the ones that are high in calories.

41:46.670 --> 41:49.256
Here, give me 50,000 won's worth.

41:49.340 --> 41:51.509
I see you still haven't learned
your lesson.

41:52.218 --> 41:53.344
You jerk…

41:53.427 --> 41:54.553
Just go!

41:54.637 --> 41:56.096
Hey.

41:56.180 --> 41:57.264
Why…

41:59.683 --> 42:01.018
Here. 100,000 won.

42:01.769 --> 42:03.187
You still won't sell them?

42:03.979 --> 42:06.982
It's 200,000 per bottle.

42:09.276 --> 42:10.486
Are you trying to get rich

42:10.569 --> 42:13.656
by selling them
in someone else's apartment?

42:13.739 --> 42:14.865
Why?

42:15.616 --> 42:17.117
Am I not allowed to get rich?

42:17.201 --> 42:19.078
I want to make money and live here too.

42:20.746 --> 42:22.164
You called me a guard dog.

42:23.958 --> 42:24.917
Go bring the money.

42:25.000 --> 42:26.001
If you don't want to,

42:26.585 --> 42:27.753
then scram!

42:31.131 --> 42:33.926
Okay, I'll just go bring more money.

42:39.431 --> 42:42.810
Did you see how he got scared
and ran away when I barked?

42:47.106 --> 42:47.982
What?

42:48.607 --> 42:50.359
Did I do something wrong?

42:50.442 --> 42:52.611
That jerk looked down on me first.

42:52.695 --> 42:53.529
No.

42:54.154 --> 42:56.156
People don't carry
that much cash these days,

42:56.865 --> 42:59.451
- so let's take jewelry as payment too.
- Right.

42:59.535 --> 43:02.830
The building representative
seems like she'd have jewelry, right?

43:02.913 --> 43:05.165
I swear I'll get them from her.

43:05.833 --> 43:08.752
With all that's going on,
we should earn as much money as we can.

43:10.421 --> 43:12.381
We have to send Seung-hui to college too.

43:16.468 --> 43:18.679
Ma'am, listen.

43:19.305 --> 43:22.224
You should stop following
the building representative's orders

43:22.308 --> 43:24.310
and clean this place instead, okay?

43:24.393 --> 43:27.354
And we're giving you expensive pastry
and water, so be thankful.

43:34.695 --> 43:38.449
Let the unjust ones commit injustice,

43:39.074 --> 43:42.161
leave the filthy ones filthy,

43:43.078 --> 43:46.749
let the just ones practice justice,

43:47.333 --> 43:49.960
and leave the holy…

43:50.044 --> 43:52.254
My arm!

43:53.881 --> 43:56.175
…ones holy.

43:56.258 --> 43:57.343
Amen.

43:59.553 --> 44:01.388
- Amen.
- Amen.

44:05.184 --> 44:08.646
Is Ms. Yoon all right?

44:08.729 --> 44:11.857
- What?
- I saw a wound on her hand.

44:12.524 --> 44:15.027
So I'm worried she might be infected.

44:15.694 --> 44:19.948
And it seemed like something was going on
with her and that military man.

44:21.992 --> 44:22.910
Right?

44:38.717 --> 44:41.011
We have flash grenades, and…

44:43.514 --> 44:44.890
You got a lot of things.

44:44.973 --> 44:46.642
We have handcuffs too.

44:52.314 --> 44:53.190
And…

44:56.026 --> 44:57.861
What is it? A walkie-talkie?

44:57.945 --> 45:00.614
He said he can't give us guns
and gave us these instead.

45:00.697 --> 45:03.158
How do I turn this thing on?
Hey, turn it on.

45:03.242 --> 45:05.536
So I can find out what's going on outside.

45:08.747 --> 45:10.791
Seo-yoon, you're here. Have some snacks.

45:11.417 --> 45:12.751
Okay.

45:15.629 --> 45:16.964
Let's do this later.

45:17.047 --> 45:19.925
If Jung-kook sees this,
I'm sure he'll feel uneasy again.

45:22.511 --> 45:23.762
Did you have a good prayer?

45:24.513 --> 45:26.348
Oh, yes.

45:34.022 --> 45:36.483
Are you worried because you can't get out?

45:37.651 --> 45:39.361
That's not why…

45:39.945 --> 45:41.196
You went outside once

45:41.280 --> 45:44.908
with Han Tae-seok,
and got blood all over your body.

45:44.992 --> 45:49.204
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

45:49.288 --> 45:50.497
I'm okay.

45:51.623 --> 45:52.749
This…

45:53.709 --> 45:55.210
When did you get this wound?

45:57.212 --> 45:58.964
I got scratched by my friend…

45:59.923 --> 46:01.300
a while ago.

46:01.383 --> 46:03.844
When you went to the dorm?

46:04.511 --> 46:07.431
Then isn't that an old wound?

46:08.182 --> 46:09.600
It won't heal easily.

46:12.519 --> 46:15.355
Mr. Kim, don't worry too much.

46:15.439 --> 46:18.442
If something happens, I'll tell you first.

46:18.525 --> 46:20.652
Come on, do you think
I'd bite you or Yi-hyun?

46:23.947 --> 46:24.990
Okay…

46:28.327 --> 46:32.748
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.

46:34.583 --> 46:35.667
And what is this one?

47:21.380 --> 47:22.631
What the heck?

47:22.714 --> 47:23.840
You got up at this hour?

47:23.924 --> 47:24.800
Sir.

47:25.384 --> 47:28.303
Please let me live here.
My mom is infected.

47:29.638 --> 47:30.722
How can I trust you?

47:31.807 --> 47:33.267
Go somewhere else.

47:33.350 --> 47:35.269
I'm really fine.

47:35.352 --> 47:37.062
I was outside all day long.

47:37.145 --> 47:38.605
And look at this.

47:40.816 --> 47:42.109
I'm really fine.

47:42.192 --> 47:44.570
I will clean, do the laundry,
and do everything else.

47:44.653 --> 47:46.196
And I brought food.

47:46.280 --> 47:47.990
I brought all the food we have.

47:48.574 --> 47:52.411
You and your wife are really nice people.
You two are very kind.

47:53.036 --> 47:54.496
Please help me.

47:57.249 --> 47:58.542
- Hang on.
- Okay.

48:01.128 --> 48:03.505
When it comes to food,
the more the better.

48:03.589 --> 48:06.174
We don't know how long
we'll have to stay here.

48:06.800 --> 48:09.136
Where would he sleep?
We don't have any extra rooms.

48:09.219 --> 48:10.721
What if he attacks us at night?

48:10.804 --> 48:13.098
- Gosh.
- I'll leave.

48:15.767 --> 48:17.185
Where would you go?

48:18.895 --> 48:21.773
I'll go to the fourth floor first.

48:22.357 --> 48:24.776
If that doesn't work,
I'll go to other units.

48:24.860 --> 48:25.777
And in return…

48:28.113 --> 48:30.782
just give me some food.

48:53.680 --> 48:54.681
Ma'am.

48:58.185 --> 48:59.936
Are you sure you're going to be okay?

49:00.020 --> 49:01.772
The other houses may not accept you.

49:03.315 --> 49:06.276
If that doesn't work,
I'll go to the basement lounge.

49:06.360 --> 49:09.237
I think it'll feel better
to stay there alone.

49:11.073 --> 49:12.032
Be careful.

49:12.908 --> 49:14.910
People are getting meaner and nastier.

49:26.713 --> 49:27.964
Thank you.

49:44.648 --> 49:45.774
What now?

49:45.857 --> 49:48.276
I found something.

49:48.360 --> 49:52.280
Something you'd be
very happy to hear about.

49:57.577 --> 49:59.121
What did you find here?

49:59.913 --> 50:02.165
Something you need right now.

50:02.249 --> 50:03.458
What's the passcode?

50:05.210 --> 50:07.003
It's 8888.

50:12.884 --> 50:16.722
Things are going well
because we're cooperating.

50:16.805 --> 50:20.267
What's in there? How do you know
when you don't even know the passcode?

50:20.350 --> 50:24.104
I saw someone
putting something in here secretly.

50:24.187 --> 50:25.605
The ones from the second floor?

50:27.441 --> 50:28.984
Did they hide food in here?

50:29.067 --> 50:30.652
You'll be shocked if you see this.

50:33.280 --> 50:34.239
Did you eat anything?

50:53.258 --> 50:54.468
Who's in there?

50:55.510 --> 50:57.596
I told you, you shouldn't live here!

51:04.853 --> 51:06.354
Mister, who are you?

51:06.438 --> 51:08.064
Let me see your face.

51:19.701 --> 51:21.328
Can anyone hear me out there?

51:22.120 --> 51:23.663
First Lieutenant Lee Ji-soo?

51:27.000 --> 51:27.959
Hey, Han Tae-seok!

51:29.211 --> 51:31.129
I'm sure they didn't give up
on this place.

51:31.213 --> 51:33.757
They probably need time
to organize things.

51:36.676 --> 51:39.554
Right, we might run out of batteries.
Let's try again later.

51:44.851 --> 51:46.770
- Hey.
- Yes?

51:46.853 --> 51:50.148
Since we're up here,
tell me about your baseball days.

51:51.483 --> 51:52.734
When I won?

51:53.401 --> 51:55.153
I got in during the third inning…

51:55.237 --> 51:56.905
Not that. Tell me about yourself.

51:57.572 --> 52:00.116
What did you depend on,
if it wasn't a religion?

52:00.200 --> 52:03.620
You said people need something
to depend on.

52:11.962 --> 52:12.796
You.

52:15.298 --> 52:17.008
- What?
- To be honest…

52:18.760 --> 52:20.303
I felt totally lost back then.

52:21.221 --> 52:23.223
I acted like I was fine in front of you.

52:23.306 --> 52:27.018
But I really thought I was nothing
when I couldn't play baseball anymore.

52:27.936 --> 52:31.231
Then after I heard what you said
and fell to the ground…

52:33.692 --> 52:35.652
I thought, "Am I going to die like this?"

52:37.571 --> 52:39.656
And suddenly, my mind was clear.

52:42.534 --> 52:44.661
I realized that it wasn't a big deal.

52:45.704 --> 52:47.581
I found peace in my heart, thanks to you.

52:49.833 --> 52:53.837
Why are you saying that in front of me?
That's embarrassing.

52:54.421 --> 52:57.257
If you're grateful,
then return the favor in secret.

52:58.842 --> 53:00.343
I've always been grateful.

53:29.664 --> 53:31.249
You two are together.

53:31.333 --> 53:33.126
- What's going on?
- Why do you care?

53:33.877 --> 53:38.715
Na Soo-min was hiding
in the apartments, infected.

53:38.798 --> 53:41.051
Is it true that you two hid him?

53:47.682 --> 53:49.851
Can I go inside for a second?

53:56.191 --> 53:57.192
Mr. Na.

53:58.318 --> 53:59.736
Can you hear us?

54:03.031 --> 54:06.451
There's no noise,
so I don't think the disease occurred.

54:19.923 --> 54:21.049
Soo-min!

54:40.360 --> 54:43.071
Mr. Na, are you okay?

54:51.246 --> 54:53.623
Please help me.

54:54.124 --> 54:58.211
I really didn't bite anyone.

54:59.087 --> 55:01.214
I only looked
at that building representative.

55:01.297 --> 55:02.674
I swear.

55:04.718 --> 55:07.679
I have to see my kids.

55:12.183 --> 55:14.853
The infected must be in quarantine, right?

55:20.859 --> 55:22.027
Just hang in there a bit.

55:22.110 --> 55:23.945
We'll check on things and be back soon.

55:24.029 --> 55:29.534
Please protect Hyun-kyung
so she won't end up like me.

55:29.617 --> 55:32.912
I didn't make the thumping sound.

55:45.216 --> 55:47.052
It's not too late.

55:53.224 --> 55:57.353
You two can be accused of being infected
because you made contact with them.

55:57.437 --> 56:00.690
I also heard you made contact with
someone in the early stages of infection.

56:00.774 --> 56:02.484
We should trust each other and--

56:02.567 --> 56:05.612
You want our support
to become the resident representative?

56:09.115 --> 56:11.659
Is this the right time to talk about that?

56:11.743 --> 56:13.369
Then when is the right time?

56:14.412 --> 56:17.082
There's no "right time" in making money.

56:22.712 --> 56:26.049
You know that Oh Joo-hyung
is a lunatic, right?

56:28.218 --> 56:32.764
How can you fight Mr. Oh
if you're so soft?

56:41.564 --> 56:43.191
Is Mr. Oh home?

56:44.025 --> 56:47.153
You should step outside for a moment.
It won't be a pretty sight.

56:54.202 --> 56:57.247
I heard you found Na Soo-min.

56:57.330 --> 57:00.250
I put in some effort
for the safety of the apartment.

57:07.715 --> 57:10.593
Drink a bottle each.

57:10.677 --> 57:13.847
I heard the infected feel more thirsty
when they drink water.

57:13.930 --> 57:17.642
You've been with Mr. Na, so I'm worried.

57:19.185 --> 57:21.521
So you're looking
for the infected among us?

57:24.357 --> 57:27.193
Then you should drink too.

58:19.913 --> 58:21.164
Thank goodness.

58:23.291 --> 58:24.834
All three of us are healthy.

58:24.918 --> 58:27.212
You should do something, Detective.

58:27.295 --> 58:31.049
That's the only way to prevent
any potential damages.

58:31.132 --> 58:33.885
You want to remain healthy
when you meet your family, right?

58:33.968 --> 58:35.094
In order to do so,

58:36.012 --> 58:39.474
you must also do
what you don't want to do.

58:40.475 --> 58:43.603
There is something you can do,
so why are you avoiding it?

58:45.855 --> 58:46.856
What…

58:47.982 --> 58:51.694
What can I do?

58:51.778 --> 58:54.364
Arrest the infected
who are pretending to be humans.

58:54.447 --> 58:57.200
And restore order here.

59:27.146 --> 59:28.648
That jerk must be throwing up.

59:29.482 --> 59:30.942
Shouldn't we throw up too?

59:32.694 --> 59:34.237
It did taste a bit bitter.

59:36.322 --> 59:38.157
I never threw up before. How do I do it?

59:38.241 --> 59:39.701
Just wait a bit.

59:49.669 --> 59:53.298
Min-ji became like that
because she took drugs, right?

59:57.135 --> 01:00:00.763
These are the drugs the fitness trainer
was secretly selling.

01:00:03.266 --> 01:00:05.059
Did you spike the drinks with this?

01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:07.812
You were the one
who put the drinks in the gym, right?

01:00:07.895 --> 01:00:10.189
To get everyone in the building infected.

01:00:10.273 --> 01:00:13.067
Because if all of the residents
either die or get the disease,

01:00:13.151 --> 01:00:15.445
you can be cleared of your murder charge.

01:00:15.528 --> 01:00:18.031
How could you come up
with such a crazy idea?

01:00:18.114 --> 01:00:19.365
No.

01:00:20.408 --> 01:00:21.909
I just need you two dead.

01:00:21.993 --> 01:00:23.786
The rest are just bonuses.

01:00:24.579 --> 01:00:27.790
More people should be infected
for the cure to come out soon.

01:00:27.874 --> 01:00:29.250
This is just ridiculous.

01:00:29.917 --> 01:00:32.003
You're confessing your crimes now, right?

01:00:32.086 --> 01:00:36.591
So just go home and never come out.

01:00:36.674 --> 01:00:38.676
If you get accused
of being infected and die,

01:00:38.760 --> 01:00:41.095
it'll just be your loss!

01:00:41.179 --> 01:00:47.143
Just stay home and live quietly
until the cure is developed, okay?

01:00:47.852 --> 01:00:50.188
You killed Park Min-ji too, right?

01:00:50.271 --> 01:00:51.481
No.

01:00:51.564 --> 01:00:53.358
I didn't kill anyone.

01:00:54.567 --> 01:01:00.281
You two should just shut up and stay home
if you don't want to kill someone.

01:01:00.365 --> 01:01:05.536
If not, just go outside and ask
that Lieutenant Colonel guy for help.

01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:06.829
But the thing is…

01:01:10.958 --> 01:01:12.043
This…

01:01:15.088 --> 01:01:16.130
What are you doing?

01:01:18.424 --> 01:01:19.550
What's wrong with you?

01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:24.806
Why did you take that? Spit it out!

01:01:26.349 --> 01:01:27.558
It's bitter.

01:01:28.142 --> 01:01:31.312
It's an indigestion reliever
I took when I played baseball.

01:01:32.897 --> 01:01:35.608
What is this? Is this food?

01:01:35.692 --> 01:01:38.986
Indigestion meds. I had a stomachache
when I was nervous about my game.

01:01:39.070 --> 01:01:43.282
I was worried about what you'd do,
so I replaced them.

01:02:17.567 --> 01:02:18.901
Damn it!

01:02:22.155 --> 01:02:25.783
And you've been caught
on the dashcam taking the drugs out.

01:02:25.867 --> 01:02:26.909
Mr. Oh,

01:02:27.952 --> 01:02:29.912
you can't get away with it this time.

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:33.249
So what?

01:02:34.083 --> 01:02:35.543
What do you mean, "so what"?

01:02:36.252 --> 01:02:38.087
A killer should be in quarantine too.

01:02:49.515 --> 01:02:50.433
Sae-bom.

01:02:52.477 --> 01:02:53.978
I'm really sorry, but…

01:02:55.521 --> 01:02:56.981
I can't get the disease.

01:02:58.441 --> 01:02:59.400
Mr. Kim.

01:03:01.277 --> 01:03:03.446
Oh Joo-hyung committed murder.

01:03:05.990 --> 01:03:07.492
That has nothing to do with us.

01:03:07.575 --> 01:03:09.952
What matters now
is if you're infected or not.

01:03:10.036 --> 01:03:12.497
You've been in contact
with the infected all this time.

01:03:12.580 --> 01:03:14.791
And Ms. Yoon, you got scratched by one.

01:03:15.833 --> 01:03:17.877
I think you two should be in quarantine.

01:03:33.518 --> 01:03:36.395
We're getting a rare shot,
so we'll get better soon.

01:03:36.479 --> 01:03:37.647
We should get well soon.

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:40.399
We're getting the shots already?

01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:41.526
This is nice.

01:03:41.609 --> 01:03:42.610
Hey.

01:03:43.110 --> 01:03:44.153
It'll be done in no time.

01:03:50.618 --> 01:03:52.995
There were a lot more infected
than I thought.

01:03:53.496 --> 01:03:56.833
Did all of you take Next?

01:03:56.916 --> 01:04:00.378
This shot greatly improved my condition.

01:04:00.461 --> 01:04:01.796
Well done.

01:04:01.879 --> 01:04:03.714
You should give it to your wife too.

01:04:03.798 --> 01:04:05.007
I should.

01:04:05.091 --> 01:04:08.469
I heard that Material 13
is hard to produce.

01:04:08.553 --> 01:04:09.387
Yes.

01:04:09.971 --> 01:04:11.180
We can't make a lot of it.

01:04:12.265 --> 01:04:15.852
We should maintain
Martial Law for a while.

01:04:15.935 --> 01:04:18.938
We must maintain the lockdown
to reduce the number of the infected,

01:04:19.021 --> 01:04:20.314
and then release the cure.

01:04:20.398 --> 01:04:25.528
It would be troublesome to let those
who may have killed someone live.

01:04:25.611 --> 01:04:26.946
You're right.

01:04:27.864 --> 01:04:30.366
Whether the issue gets solved or not,

01:04:30.449 --> 01:04:33.035
it's better to get rid of those
who may cause problems.

01:04:35.496 --> 01:04:36.747
People like you.

01:04:38.749 --> 01:04:40.209
What are you talking about?

01:04:40.293 --> 01:04:42.503
You took the cure
that just began clinical trials

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:44.714
by using your money and power.

01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:47.675
You should be responsible
for your wrongdoings.

01:04:51.554 --> 01:04:53.347
What are you going to do about it?

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:38.059
Thanks to all of you,
I can get more help in collecting data.

01:05:53.658 --> 01:05:55.201
Have a good time.

01:06:25.106 --> 01:06:29.360
WONJUNG DORMITORY

01:06:30.486 --> 01:06:33.990
Lieutenant Colonel,
there's a problem at the CEO's ward.

01:06:34.073 --> 01:06:36.909
A mass infection among
the politicians in high positions…

01:06:36.993 --> 01:06:40.204
They stole Candidate Material 13
and got injected with it.

01:06:42.081 --> 01:06:44.709
But that failed
at the second clinical stage.

01:06:45.543 --> 01:06:47.628
We were discarding all of it…

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:49.005
I guess they didn't know.

01:06:51.132 --> 01:06:54.510
They're in high positions,
so tell them to capture them alive.

01:06:54.593 --> 01:06:57.096
We have to use them
as clinical test subjects.

01:07:24.957 --> 01:07:26.000
Honey.

01:07:30.755 --> 01:07:32.298
I'm thirsty.

01:07:33.549 --> 01:07:34.550
Young-in.

01:07:38.179 --> 01:07:39.555
We're almost there now.

01:08:15.007 --> 01:08:17.384
I'm running out of patience.

01:08:18.969 --> 01:08:20.679
Are you thirsty too?

01:08:20.763 --> 01:08:24.350
They hide their thirst well,
and we can't tell just by looking.

01:08:24.433 --> 01:08:28.646
Be careful.
You must never trust those people.

01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:31.524
Should we look for the infected?

01:08:31.607 --> 01:08:35.528
You just need to say the woman
on the fifth floor seems infected.

01:08:36.695 --> 01:08:38.906
When I'm in danger,
I'll take that drug too.

01:08:38.989 --> 01:08:41.325
I'm sure there will be casualties.

01:08:41.408 --> 01:08:42.660
I only have one choice.

01:08:42.743 --> 01:08:44.578
You killed him.

01:08:48.415 --> 01:08:53.420
Subtitle translation by: Hae-lim Lee
